{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781183658,"nonce":"oztKLcJBzOp0VYPxiTPw1FU8jaU=","title":"rANS extraction crash (L6-9) + \u003e64KB silent corruption: master method field, EOB desync, bits_feed overread","message":"Found while debugging 'uc2 extraction error on sdf.org' (NetBSD 10/gcc 7.5); reproduced on Linux — not platform-specific.\n\nFour related defects, all fixed:\n\n1. cli/src/main.c master entry hardcoded method=1 in the COMPRESS record while master data was compressed with uc2_compress_ex(opt.level) — at L6-9 the data is rANS (method 10), so extraction ran the Huffman decoder over rANS bits. Now records 10 for level \u003e= 6 (1 kept for \u003c= 5: original UC2 Pro compat, methods 1-9 share the Huffman bitstream).\n\n2. decompressor_rans() exited its symbol loop at remaining==0, leaving the trailing EOB pair and its 12 extra bits unconsumed — every bounded rANS decode left the bit cursor 12 bits short, and the next block-present read saw the MSB of the EOB extras (always 1), parsing a phantom block (observed: nsyms=16416=0x4020). Benign or fatal depending on trailing archive bytes. The loop now decodes all nsyms symbols; literal/match writes are guarded by remaining.\n\n3. bits_feed() refill: a read returning 1 byte into an empty buffer let head (2) overtake tail (1); unsigned tail-head wrapped huge, refills stopped, and head marched past the 4096-byte buffer (ASan: stack/heap-buffer-overflow; NetBSD: Memory fault, Linux Release: SIGSEGV at stack guard). Refill now loops until a full 2-byte pair is buffered, with a sticky err flag; decompressor_rans checks it at block boundaries instead of treating negative bits_get returns as data (the old 'while (bits_get(\u0026bi,1))' treated errors as block-present).\n\n4. Pre-existing \u003e64KB silent corruption at ALL levels (exit 0, wrong bytes from ~byte 4): uc2_compress_ex loaded chunks linearly at c-\u003edata+load_pos without capping at the 64KB window edge — any master-misaligned load crossing the edge overflowed the buffer and lost the wrap region. Also decompressor_rans flushed output once at the end via a linear write that cannot represent ring wrap (\u003e32KB-master + file crossing the edge, or any \u003e64KB output). Chunk loads are now capped at the edge; the rANS decoder flushes incrementally in ring order (rans_flush, 32KB threshold; max match 35482 \u003c 64000 window margin holds).\n\nVerification: 102/102 local round-trips (21 files x L2/5/6/9 solo, thresholds 65535-200000, 8-level multifile incl. 65535-byte master and 300-540KB files), ASan/UBSan clean, ctest 21/21 incl. roundtrip_dosbox (original UC2 Pro compat preserved), NetBSD rie: 8 levels x 21 files + big files + NFS-home extraction all clean. Archives written by the buggy writer extract correctly with the fixed reader (garbage master decode is contained and unreferenced in tested corpus).\n\nAlso fixed: BCJ E8/E9 byte-assembly UB (uint8_t promoted/shifted into sign bit) in uc2_preprocess.c; libarchive plugin dos_to_unix_time now uses timegm on NetBSD/OpenBSD/DragonFly instead of mktime (timestamps were offset by timezone).","files":null}]}